-- ccc10-marriage.l4 -- sections 287 to 296 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: abortion, venereal diseases and conjugal rights
-- (the repealed sections 287, 288, 289 and 296; bigamy, feigned marriage, polygamy, forced marriage, marriage under 16, and unlawful solemnization).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (every element holds, or the defence or rule applies); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in the branch's comment);
-- NOTHING (not covered: an element is missing, the text is silent or limits a prohibition in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seam: `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's answer.

