§ `s 290 -- Bigamy`

-- 290(1): "commits bigamy who (a) in Canada, (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ...; or (b) being a Canadian citizen resident in Canada leaves Canada with intent ...".
-- src:5855 | 290 (1) Every one commits bigamy who
-- src:5856 | (a) in Canada,
-- src:5857 | (i) being married, goes through a form of marriage with another person,
-- src:5858 | (ii) knowing that another person is married, goes through a form of marriage with that person, or
-- src:5859 | (iii) on the same day or simultaneously, goes through a form of marriage with more than one person; or
-- src:5860 | (b) being a Canadian citizen resident in Canada leaves Canada with intent to do anything mentioned in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii) and, pursuant thereto, does outside Canada anything mentioned in those subparagraphs in circumstances mentioned therein.
@ref s 290(1) (src:5855-5860)
GIVEN `the person acts in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, being married, goes through a form of marriage with another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, knowing that another person is married, goes through a form of marriage with that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, on the same day or simultaneously, goes through a form of marriage with more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian citizen resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person leaves Canada with intent to do anything mentioned in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pursuant to that intent, the person does outside Canada anything mentioned in those subparagraphs in circumstances mentioned therein` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 290(1) the person commits bigamy` MEANS
    IF    (`the person acts in Canada` AND (`the person, being married, goes through a form of marriage with another person` OR `the person, knowing that another person is married, goes through a form of marriage with that person` OR `the person, on the same day or simultaneously, goes through a form of marriage with more than one person`))
       OR (`the person is a Canadian citizen resident in Canada` AND `the person leaves Canada with intent to do anything mentioned in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii)` AND `pursuant to that intent, the person does outside Canada anything mentioned in those subparagraphs in circumstances mentioned therein`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits bigamy who" acts in Canada as (a)(i) to (iii) or, being a Canadian citizen resident in Canada, as (b)

-- 290(2): "No person commits bigamy by going through a form of marriage if" one of four things. The function answers JUST TRUE when one holds and JUST FALSE when none does
-- (a failed "if", marginal reading (a)). Paragraph (b): seven years continuously absent immediately before, unless the person knew the spouse was alive in that time.
-- src:5861 | Matters of defence
-- src:5862 | (2) No person commits bigamy by going through a form of marriage if
-- src:5863 | (a) that person in good faith and on reasonable grounds believes that his spouse is dead;
-- src:5864 | (b) the spouse of that person has been continuously absent from him for seven years immediately preceding the time when he goes through the form of marriage, unless he knew that his spouse was alive at any time during those seven years;
-- src:5865 | (c) that person has been divorced from the bond of the first marriage; or
-- src:5866 | (d) the former marriage has been declared void by a court of competent jurisdiction.
@ref s 290(2) (src:5861-5866)
GIVEN `the person in good faith and on reasonable grounds believes that their spouse is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the spouse’s continuous absence began` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person goes through the form of marriage` IS A DATE
      `the person knew that the spouse was alive at any time during those seven years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been divorced from the bond of the first marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the former marriage has been declared void by a court of competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 290(2) the person does not commit bigamy by going through the form of marriage` MEANS
    IF    `the person in good faith and on reasonable grounds believes that their spouse is dead`
       OR (`the spouse has been continuously absent for seven years` AND (NOT `the person knew that the spouse was alive at any time during those seven years`))
       OR `the person has been divorced from the bond of the first marriage`
       OR `the former marriage has been declared void by a court of competent jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits bigamy by going through a form of marriage if" (none of (a) to (d) holds: a failed "if", marginal reading (a); this section gives no defence on these facts)
    WHERE
        -- seven years continuously absent immediately preceding the form of marriage: the day seven years after the absence began has been reached
        `the spouse has been continuously absent for seven years` MEANS
            (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person goes through the form of marriage`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL (Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the spouse’s continuous absence began`) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the spouse’s continuous absence began`) ((DATE_YEAR `the day on which the spouse’s continuous absence began`) PLUS 7)))

-- The offence of 290(1) after the matters of defence of 290(2): a defence that applies is the text's no ("No person commits bigamy").
@ref s 290(1) composed with s 290(2) (src:5861-5866)
GIVEN `the answer of s 290(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 290(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 290 the person commits bigamy after the matters of defence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 290(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits bigamy by going through a form of marriage if"
        IF (`the answer of s 290(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 290(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence or the matters of defence are not covered

-- src:5867 | Incompetency no defence
-- src:5868 | (3) Where a person is alleged to have committed bigamy, it is not a defence that the parties would, if unmarried, have been incompetent to contract marriage under the law of the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed.
@ref s 290(3) (src:5867-5868)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have committed bigamy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties would, if unmarried, have been incompetent to contract marriage under the law of the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 290(3) the incompetence of the parties to contract marriage is a defence` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have committed bigamy` AND `the parties would, if unmarried, have been incompetent to contract marriage under the law of the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not a defence that the parties would, if unmarried, have been incompetent to contract marriage under the law of the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is alleged to have committed bigamy"

-- 290(4): "deemed to be valid unless the accused establishes that it was invalid": the "unless" met gives JUST FALSE (fork F3's reading).
-- src:5869 | Validity presumed
-- src:5870 | (4) Every marriage or form of marriage shall, for the purpose of this section, be deemed to be valid unless the accused establishes that it was invalid.
@ref s 290(4) (src:5869-5870)
GIVEN `the accused establishes that the marriage or form of marriage was invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 290(4) the marriage or form of marriage is deemed to be valid` MEANS
    IF `the accused establishes that the marriage or form of marriage was invalid`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused establishes that it was invalid"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5871 | Act or omission by accused
-- src:5872 | (5) No act or omission on the part of an accused who is charged with bigamy invalidates a marriage or form of marriage that is otherwise valid.
@ref s 290(5) (src:5871-5872)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with bigamy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage or form of marriage is otherwise valid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is on the part of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 290(5) an act or omission of the accused invalidates the marriage or form of marriage` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with bigamy` AND `the marriage or form of marriage is otherwise valid` AND `the act or omission is on the part of the accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No act or omission on the part of an accused who is charged with bigamy invalidates a marriage or form of marriage that is otherwise valid"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused who is charged with bigamy" and a marriage "that is otherwise valid"

§ `s 291 -- Punishment of bigamy`

-- src:5874 | 291 (1) Every person who commits bigamy is guilty of
-- src:5875 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5876 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 291(1) (src:5874-5876)
GIVEN `the answer of s 290` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(1) the person who commits bigamy is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 290` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who commits bigamy is guilty of"

@ref s 291(1) (src:5874-5876)
`s 291(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 291(1) (src:5875-5876)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 291(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

