§ `ss 294 to 296 -- Unlawful solemnization of marriage`

-- src:5901 | Pretending to solemnize marriage
-- src:5902 | 294 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:5903 | (a) solemnizes or pretends to solemnize a marriage without lawful authority; or
-- src:5904 | (b) procures a person to solemnize a marriage knowing that he is not lawfully authorized to solemnize the marriage.
@ref s 294 (src:5901-5904)
GIVEN `the person solemnizes or pretends to solemnize a marriage without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person procures a person to solemnize a marriage knowing that the person is not lawfully authorized to solemnize the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 294 the person is guilty of the offence of pretending to solemnize marriage` MEANS
    IF `the person solemnizes or pretends to solemnize a marriage without lawful authority` OR `the person procures a person to solemnize a marriage knowing that the person is not lawfully authorized to solemnize the marriage`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who (a) solemnizes or pretends to solemnize a marriage without lawful authority" or "(b) procures a person to solemnize a marriage knowing that he is not lawfully authorized"

@ref s 294 (src:5901-5904)
`s 294 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 294 (src:5902)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
